    "updated_at": "2024-03-22T13:54:45Z",
    "body": "What should I do?\r\n\r\nI didn’t do on purpose\r\nSent from my iPhone\r\n\r\nOn Mar 22, 2024, at 9:54 AM, Jake Archibald ***@***.***> wrote:\r\n\r\n﻿\r\n\r\nWhat problem are you trying to solve?\r\n\r\nI want to create a custom element, <ui-form>, which has or wraps form functionality.\r\n\r\nWhat solutions exist today?\r\n\r\n<form is=\"my-custom-thing\">, but WebKit opposes this<https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/97>.\r\n\r\nHow would you solve it?\r\n\r\nAssuming that WebKit will not change their position:\r\n\r\nMy <ui-form> could create a shadow root which contains <form><slot></slot></form>.\r\n\r\nHowever, at present (although it isn't clear from the algorithm<https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#reset-the-form-owner>), shadow boundaries are not crossed when associating fields with forms.\r\n\r\nInstead, the algorithm<https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#reset-the-form-owner> could be updated to cross-shadow boundaries. For compatibility, the form must opt-in to being considered when crossing shadow boundaries: <form allowcrossshadowboundarypleasethankyou>. There may be better names.\r\n\r\nAnything else?\r\n\r\nNo response\r\n\r\n—\r\nReply to this email directly, view it on GitHub<https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10220>, or unsubscribe<https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/BGAE5QWRN64U7PVVITQYGK3YZQZXLAVCNFSM6AAAAABFDL2O2WVHI2DSMVQWIX3LMV43ASLTON2WKOZSGIYDENJUHE3DQMA>.\r\nYou are receiving this because you are subscribed to this thread.Message ID: ***@***.***>\r\n",
